<blockquote>
  <blockquote>
    <blockquote>
      <p align="center"><b><font size="5" color="#F3DAE0" face="Arial">Dreamweavers
      Rules of Conduct</font></b></p>
      <p align="center"><img border="0" src="graphicsbar.gif"></p>
      <p align="left"><b><font color="#F3DAE0" face="Arial" size="5"><u>In
      General:</u></font></b></p>
      <p align="left"><i><b><font size="4" color="#F3DAE0">Thou shall not Steal
      Kills.</font></b></i></p>
      <p align="left"><i><b><font size="4" color="#F3DAE0">Thou shall not Take
      Over Other’s spawns (camps) without allowing others to kill the spawn
      first or without asking to share first.</font></b></i></p>
      <p align="left"><i><b><font size="4" color="#F3DAE0">Thou shall not use
      foul language.</font></b></i></p>
      <p align="left"><i><b><font size="4" color="#F3DAE0">Thou shall not scam
      other players to take their stuff.</font></b></i></p>
      <p align="left"><i><b><font size="4" color="#F3DAE0">You should treat
      others how you wish to be treated.</font></b></i></p>
      <p align="left"><i><b><font size="4" color="#F3DAE0">Remember, guild
      members you help may quickly be in a position to help you!</font></b></i></p>
      <p align="left"><i><b><font size="4" color="#F3DAE0">And always try to
      group with family.&nbsp; In raids and in groups, family comes first.&nbsp;</font></b></i></p>
      <p align="left"><font color="#F3DAE0">&nbsp;<b><font color="#FFDEAD" face="Arial" size="5"><u>Raiding
      Rules:</u> </font></b></font></p>
      <p align="left"><i><b><font size="4" color="#F3DAE0">Raids are established
      for a purpose... usually experience/gear or for Quest Items. Know why you
      are on the raid!</font></b></i></p>
      <p align="left"><i><b><font size="4" color="#F3DAE0">Raids will be shown
      on Calendar, Announced in Weekly Newsletters, Posted on the Message Boards
      and Posted in the Guild M.O.T.D!</font></b></i></p>
      <p align="left"><i><b><font size="4" color="#F3DAE0">If you wish to join a
      certain raid, make sure you are on site before the raid is scheduled to
      begin. </font></b></i></p>
      <p align="left"><i><b><font size="4" color="#F3DAE0">Listen to your Raid
      Leader in the Channel He or She has set up! The Raid Leader has last say
      over how the raid is to be held. </font></b></i></p>
      <p align="left"><i><b><font size="4" color="#F3DAE0">The Raid Leader will
      not only assign members to groups, and the Group Leader, but also list
      rules for that raid and how loot will be divvied up!</font></b></i></p>
      <p align="left"><i><b><font size="4" color="#F3DAE0">The Group Leader
      should keep track of their members and if there are concerns about XP or
      Loot etc., members should ask the Group Leader - who IN TURN will ask the
      Raid Leader.</font></b></i></p>
      <p align="left"><i><b><font size="4" color="#F3DAE0">Raid leaders will
      choose Guild members over other characters wanting to join the raid</font><font size="4" color="#90A8D0">.</font></b></i></p>
      <p align="left"><font color="#F3DAE0"><b><font color="#FFDEAD" face="Arial" size="5"><u>Loot
      Rules:</u> </font></b></font></p>
      <p align="left"><i><b><font size="4" color="#F3DAE0">The Guild operates on
      a </font><font color="#F3DAE0" size="5">Need before Greed</font><font size="4" color="#F3DAE0">
      basis!&nbsp;</font></b></i></p>
      <p align="left"><i><b><font size="4" color="#F3DAE0">Members with
      seniority, playing their Mains are allowed first choice if an item is
      dropped that their Main can use.&nbsp;</font></b></i></p>
      <p align="left"><i><b><font size="4" color="#F3DAE0">If there is no
      seniority, the item is given to the player class that can use it. If more
      than one member has the same class, it's rolled for.&nbsp;</font></b></i></p>
      <p align="left"><i><b><font size="4" color="#F3DAE0">If all members can
      use it, the item is then rolled for at then end of that raid.&nbsp; You
      have to stay in the raid if you want loot at the end of it!</font></b></i></p>
      <p align="left"><i><b><font size="4" color="#F3DAE0">In the case of
      duplicate items being dropped, the person who has one already, is exempt
      from rolling on it again.&nbsp;</font></b></i></p>
      <p align="left"><i><b><font size="4" color="#F3DAE0">If the item is No
      Drop, it's rolled for before decay - by members who can use it with the
      character at the raid.&nbsp;</font></b></i></p>
      <p align="left"><i><b><font size="4" color="#F3DAE0">Platinum will be
      collected, and at the end of the raid&nbsp;&nbsp; be distributed by
      the Raid Leader.&nbsp;</font></b></i></p>
      <p align="left"><i><b><font size="4" color="#F3DAE0">Of course, loot that
      is for an Epic or Quest that a member is doing is exempt.&nbsp;</font></b></i></p>
      <p align="left"><i><b><font size="4" color="#F3DAE0">Ninja Looting is not
      tolerated nor honorable.&nbsp; Dreamweavers wants all of our members to
      prosper, but not at the sake of depriving other members.</font></b></i></p>
      <p align="left"><font color="#F3DAE0"><u><b><font color="#FFDEAD" face="Arial" size="5">Dispute
      Rules: </font></b></u></font></p>
      <p align="left"><i><b><font size="4" color="#F3DAE0">If you have
      questions, concerns or trouble: Instead off&nbsp; discussing in guild say
      /the message boards, or leaving the guild,&nbsp; Members should contact an
      officer online as soon as possible. </font></b></i></p>
      <p align="left"><i><b><font size="4" color="#F3DAE0">Members who leave the
      guild are allowed to return one time.&nbsp; </font></b></i></p>
      <p align="left"><i><b><font size="4" color="#F3DAE0">If a member leaves
      again, to return they need to speak to an officer and their situation will
      be discussed by the Round Table who will vote weather or not to invite
      again.</font></b></i></p>
      <p align="center"><img border="0" src="graphicsbar.gif"></p>
    </blockquote>
  </blockquote>
</blockquote>

